Command lineLibrary <pre><code>cargo binstall chloro          # or: cargo install chloro --features cli
chloro --check src/            # exit 1 if any file would change
chloro --write src/            # format in place
</code></pre> <pre><code>let formatted = chloro::format_source("fn main(){let x=1;}");
assert_eq!(formatted, "fn main() {\n    let x = 1;\n}\n");
</code></pre>

CLIBy nameBy field <pre><code>chloro --config max_width=80,use_small_heuristics=Max --write src/
</code></pre> <p><code>--config</code> takes comma-separated <code>key=value</code> pairs, as rustfmt's <code>--config</code> does. Values may be quoted (<code>edition="2021"</code>).</p> <pre><code>let mut config = chloro::Config::default();
config.set("max_width", "80").unwrap();
config.set("use_small_heuristics", "Max").unwrap();
let formatted = chloro::format_source_with_config("fn main() {}\n", &amp;config);
</code></pre> <p><code>Config::set</code> takes the same names and spellings as <code>--config</code> and returns an error message for an unknown option or an invalid value.</p> <pre><code>let config = chloro::Config {
    max_width: 80,
    tab_spaces: 2,
    ..chloro::Config::default()
};
let formatted = chloro::format_source_with_config("fn main() {}\n", &amp;config);
</code></pre> <p>Every stable option is a public field of <code>Config</code>. The enum-valued fields (<code>newline_style</code>, <code>edition</code>, …) take types from <code>chloro_core::formatter::config</code>.</p> <p>chloro does not read <code>rustfmt.toml</code> or <code>.rustfmt.toml</code>. A project that has one can pass its stable options through <code>--config</code>:</p> rustfmt.toml<pre><code>max_width = 120
use_field_init_shorthand = true
</code></pre> <pre><code>chloro --config max_width=120,use_field_init_shorthand=true --check src/
</code></pre>
